        excerpt: "Federal programs, regional marathons, personal contact with entrepreneurs and smart GR — a formula that works at country scale.",
        body: "Growing a seller base by 350% isn't the result of one clever channel. It's a three-layer operational formula, plus two factors that rarely make it into case studies but matter just as much in practice: personal contact with entrepreneurs, and a systematic relationship with government.\n\n## Layer one: institutional partnerships\n\nRegional \"My Business\" support centers across 86 regions gave access to an audience already thinking about going online but unsure where to start — a pre-filtered base, not cold traffic. Over two years, more than 50,000 sellers passed through this funnel.\n\n## Layer two: event marketing\n\nMarathons across 20 cities solved something a banner ad can't: a live walkthrough of the platform, answers to a specific seller's specific questions, and social proof from other local entrepreneurs in the room. One event on average closed a question that would have taken three weeks of back-and-forth in chat.\n\n## Layer three: product triggers\n\nOnboarding built so a seller reaches their first sale in 7 days, not 7 weeks — because sign-up motivation fades fast if there's no visible result right away.\n\n## The invisible line: staying close to the entrepreneur\n\nThere's something hard to put a metric on, but without it the formula doesn't work: personal contact with sellers, regardless of title. Whether you're the boss or a senior manager, if you don't hear your \"electorate\" — the entrepreneurs on the ground — directly, your strategy is built on guesses, not real problems. I made a point of direct contact regularly: not through reports or third parties, but in person — at marathons, on calls, on regional ground. Half of the product hypotheses that actually worked came from exactly there.\n\n## The Ministry of Economic Development and GR as an asset, not a formality\n\nThere's a growth source that rarely gets said out loud: a properly built relationship with the Ministry of Economic Development gives a real boost — not just audience access through the \"My Business\" centers, but a status that removes half the entrepreneur's doubts at the start. GR support in this combination isn't about paperwork — it's about reliability: the seller and the team always have somewhere to go with a specific question and get a specific answer, not a promise to call back. That trust converts into faster decisions on the ground — and, in turn, into conversion.\n\n## Why it's a flywheel, not a funnel\n\nEach layer reinforces the next: partnerships bring quality traffic, events convert it into sign-ups, product triggers carry it through to a first sale, and personal contact plus GR support hold the whole system together on trust, not ad spend. That's why the growth was compounding — 350% from a combination that can't be replicated piece by piece.",
